Obligations:
  [functional/explicit] obligation-flat-obligations-and-open-questions: `decompose` returns two flat outputs: a flat list of obligations and a flat list of open questions.  <- task
  [invariant/explicit] obligation-cover-all-requirements: Every requirement in a task file is represented in the decomposition result through exactly one disposition.  <- task, completion-02
  [functional/explicit] obligation-requirement-registry-from-parser: The requirement registry is derived from `requirement/task_file.py::parse_task_file`.  <- constraint-01
  [invariant/explicit] obligation-requirement-ids-assigned-by-code: Requirement ids are assigned by the code rather than by the model.  <- constraint-02, completion-07
  [functional/explicit] obligation-requirement-id-section-ordinal-parse-order: A requirement id is formed from its section and its ordinal within that section, in parse order.  <- constraint-03, completion-07
  [functional/explicit] obligation-registry-entry-textspan: Each registry entry carries the `TextSpan` of the requirement it identifies.  <- constraint-04
  [functional/explicit] obligation-many-to-many-requirement-obligation-link: The requirement-to-obligation relation is many-to-many, and an obligation serving two requirements is linked to both.  <- constraint-05, constraint-06, constraint-07, completion-05, completion-06
  [invariant/explicit] obligation-single-disposition-per-requirement: Every requirement carries exactly one disposition.  <- constraint-08, completion-03
  [functional/explicit] obligation-disposition-kinds: The disposition set consists of yielded obligations, deliberately yields none with a reason, or raised an open question instead.  <- constraint-09
  [functional/explicit] obligation-mapping-persisted-in-review-state: The requirement-to-obligation mapping is persisted in the structured review state defined by `review_state.py` and `review_store.py`.  <- constraint-10, completion-10
  [functional/explicit] obligation-mapping-rendered-in-section-16-report: The requirement-to-obligation mapping is rendered in the §16 report.  <- constraint-11, completion-04
  [functional/explicit] obligation-user-prompt-typed-identified-fields: `requirement/obligations.py::_user_prompt` passes typed, identified fields.  <- constraint-12
  [invariant/explicit] obligation-user-prompt-omits-parsed-source: `_user_prompt` excludes `parsed.source` from the data it passes.  <- constraint-13
  [compatibility/explicit] obligation-decomposer-no-changeset: The decomposer receives no `ChangeSet`.  <- constraint-14, completion-08
  [compatibility/explicit] obligation-decomposer-no-repo-path: The decomposer receives no repository path.  <- constraint-15
  [compatibility/explicit] obligation-decomposer-no-head-revision: The decomposer receives no head revision.  <- constraint-16, completion-09
  [compatibility/explicit] obligation-typed-schemas-are-pydantic: Typed schemas are implemented as pydantic models.  <- constraint-17
  [regression/explicit] obligation-tests-no-live-model-calls: Tests issue no live model calls.  <- constraint-18
  [regression/explicit] obligation-recorded-transcripts-rerecorded-on-prompt-change: Recorded transcripts invalidated by the changed prompt are re-recorded once.  <- constraint-19, completion-11, completion-12
  [compatibility/explicit] obligation-obligation-content-fixed-representation-changes: The obligation content remains fixed while its representation changes.  <- exclusion-01
  [human_review/explicit] obligation-open-question-no-citation-required: An open question does not need to cite where the task file fails to answer it.  <- exclusion-04
  [docs_config/explicit] obligation-docs-record-resolved-requirement-id-decision: `docs/DR-202-decomposition-requirement-mapping.md` records the resolved requirement-id decision in place of listing it as open.  <- completion-13
  [docs_config/explicit] obligation-docs-mark-accuracy-non-comparable: The decomposition-accuracy figure is marked non-comparable across this change where a reader encounters it.  <- completion-14

